WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.250
In 2024, nearly 138 million
children were in child labour.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:12.070
About 54 million did hazardous work,
likely to harm their health or safety.

3
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.070
Nearly a third of child labourers
of school age miss class.

4
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.850
For children who don't
work, it's 8 per cent.

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.790
So why do so many children
work instead of learning?

6
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.890
Do they just find school boring?

7
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.090
Do laws make them work?

8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.950
In this mission, you'll find
out what counts as child labour,

9
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.450
and why children end up in it.

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.910
Then you'll judge which plans
really get children back into class.

11
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.690
Your mission: find out why children
work instead of going to school,

12
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.530
and what brings them back.
